WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.254
When oxygen, heat and fuel combine,
we get fire.

00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:05.964
It's basic.

00:00:05.964 --> 00:00:07.090
It's primal.

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:10.093
And is the key that unlocked
human progress.

00:00:10.385 --> 00:00:14.931
Fire provided
light and heat and protection. With fire

00:00:14.931 --> 00:00:18.476
our ancestors could move to new climates
and eat new foods.

00:00:19.102 --> 00:00:23.565
Pottery, metallurgy,
chemistry, rapid transportation

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:27.235
and many other technologies
all start with fire.

00:00:28.111 --> 00:00:31.114
But imagine if fire had been proprietary.

00:00:31.406 --> 00:00:34.409
What if that knowledge hadn't been shared?

00:00:34.617 --> 00:00:37.704
What if there had been
just a few keepers of the fire?

00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:39.497
What would we be?

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.933
My name is Dario Gil

00:00:58.933 --> 00:01:03.188
and I'm senior vice president
at IBM and a director of IBM Research.

00:01:04.355 --> 00:01:07.358
We are in a landmark moment
now with generative AI

00:01:07.442 --> 00:01:10.945
that will shape our society
for generations to come.

00:01:11.821 --> 00:01:16.159
In this episode, I'm going to show you
why you need to be your own

00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:20.622
AI firestarter,
how to take control of your AI destiny,

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:25.126
to go from being just an AI user
to become an AI value creator.

00:01:25.877 --> 00:01:31.299
Chances are you're already an AI user,
even if you don't have a formal

00:01:31.508 --> 00:01:36.638
AI initiative or an AI team in place,
it's already in use across your business.

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:40.433
It might be baked into your off the shelf
applications.

00:01:40.725 --> 00:01:42.894
It may show up in chat bots, in H.R.

00:01:42.894 --> 00:01:45.897
self-service portals, and transcription
services.

00:01:46.689 --> 00:01:49.692
These are what we might call
traditional AI.

00:01:50.026 --> 00:01:54.989
The focus is on executing discrete tasks,
and usually each instance is trained

00:01:54.989 --> 00:01:58.910
individually on its own data
that you have to compile and label.

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:03.039
Now, what makes Generative AI different
is that it is enormously flexible

00:02:03.248 --> 00:02:06.042
and not limited to narrow tasks.

00:02:06.042 --> 00:02:09.003
Think of it as instead of filling
specific blanks,

00:02:09.003 --> 00:02:12.966
it can write the whole document
from scratch to the point of being able

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:16.094
to create or generate
something entirely new.

00:02:16.845 --> 00:02:18.388
What makes this possible,

00:02:18.388 --> 00:02:20.473
are foundation models.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:24.102
Foundation models aren’t trained
the same way as traditional AI.

00:02:24.769 --> 00:02:27.772
They're trained
using self-supervised learning.

00:02:28.106 --> 00:02:31.234
You don't have to manually annotate
a massive amount of data.

00:02:32.026 --> 00:02:35.738
You tell them to go read
enormous amounts of text, and they do.

00:02:36.406 --> 00:02:39.367
And you end up with a large
but versatile model

00:02:39.576 --> 00:02:42.579
with more humanlike language capabilities.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:45.874
Algorithms use mathematical models
to represent

00:02:45.874 --> 00:02:49.002
the relationships
between the words they ingest.

00:02:49.711 --> 00:02:52.297
If you give the model
a few words in a prompt,

00:02:52.297 --> 00:02:56.176
you can mathematically predict
the likelihood of words in the response.

00:02:57.051 --> 00:02:58.803
Instead of needing to build one A.I.

00:02:58.803 --> 00:03:02.932
model for each specific task,
you can train one model

00:03:02.932 --> 00:03:06.811
and adapt it to many varied
downstream tasks.

00:03:07.478 --> 00:03:11.149
So we went from one
task, one model to one model,

00:03:11.149 --> 00:03:12.817
many tasks.

00:03:12.817 --> 00:03:15.403
Your chat bot and your H.R. self-service

00:03:15.403 --> 00:03:18.406
can be built on the same model
as the new app

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:22.327
that will write your marketing emails
and summarize legal documents.

00:03:23.077 --> 00:03:25.663
So that's the first critical point.

00:03:25.663 --> 00:03:28.958
Ideally,
a model is in the final form of AI.

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:31.169
It's just a foundation you build on.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:33.922
How you use it is up to you.

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:40.094
When it comes to using AI,

00:03:40.094 --> 00:03:43.223
there are basically three modes
of consumption.

00:03:43.973 --> 00:03:45.725
The first is embedded AI,

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:50.230
which I already mentioned,
is baked in to off the shelf software.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:53.775
The software vendor creates the AI

00:03:53.775 --> 00:03:56.402
and you put it to use in your business.

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:59.572
Whether it's a writing a system
that can help you strike the right

00:03:59.614 --> 00:04:02.575
tone in your email or image
editing software

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:05.161
that can automatically process
your images,

00:04:05.161 --> 00:04:07.956
you get access to some great functionality

00:04:07.956 --> 00:04:11.084
that can make you more productive,
which we always want.

00:04:12.043 --> 00:04:14.712
But the caveat is that what you can buy

00:04:14.712 --> 00:04:17.590
so can everybody else. Those capabilities

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:21.010
and productivity opportunities
don't become differentiators.

00:04:21.469 --> 00:04:25.056
They set a new higher baseline
for everyone.

00:04:25.807 --> 00:04:29.269
The second mode of consumption
is through API calls.

00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:32.730
As you develop
custom applications for your business,

00:04:33.064 --> 00:04:36.276
they can call out to another company’s
AI service

00:04:36.651 --> 00:04:41.364
using that company's models and processes
and then return the results.

00:04:41.739 --> 00:04:44.742
This is also a valuable way
of consuming AI,

00:04:45.076 --> 00:04:48.871
depending on how cleverly you use the APIs
and the diversity

00:04:48.871 --> 00:04:51.165
of AI service providers you use.

00:04:51.165 --> 00:04:56.045
You can start to differentiate how you put
AI to work relative to your competitors.

00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:59.257
But there are caveats here too.

00:04:59.257 --> 00:05:01.801
The first is that, like with software,

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:06.014
the models and services
you tap into are available to everyone.

00:05:06.597 --> 00:05:09.642
The second is
that when that API call goes out,

00:05:10.018 --> 00:05:13.021
it's connecting to
what looks like a black box.

00:05:13.104 --> 00:05:16.107
You don't necessarily know
what's happening on the other end

00:05:16.399 --> 00:05:19.402
or the provenance
and governance of the data use,

00:05:19.944 --> 00:05:22.822
which can make people nervous
because your business

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:25.825
is still accountable
for the final outcomes.

00:05:25.867 --> 00:05:29.495
And a second word of caution
when using someone else's

00:05:29.704 --> 00:05:33.750
AI, has to do with the creation
and accrual of value over the long term.

00:05:34.542 --> 00:05:38.546
In the past, we've seen a lot of value
extractive business models.

00:05:39.297 --> 00:05:42.425
Another company would offer you a service
like this API call

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:44.677
and you get value from that.

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:47.138
But the other company
is also extracting value

00:05:47.138 --> 00:05:51.059
from your usage and from your data
accumulating more and more.

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:54.812
How much faster is their value
growing than yours?

00:05:54.812 --> 00:05:57.815
Well, you can see it in the stock
prices over time.

00:05:58.775 --> 00:06:01.778
There is an imbalance in the relationship,

00:06:01.986 --> 00:06:06.407
that can have long term consequences
both for your specific business

00:06:06.616 --> 00:06:09.786
and for the overall economy
and progress of technology.

00:06:11.496 --> 00:06:14.207
This goes back to the metaphor
I used earlier.

00:06:14.207 --> 00:06:19.087
Philosophically, do we as a society
really want just a few keepers of the fire

00:06:19.504 --> 00:06:22.173
upon which we are all dependent?

00:06:22.173 --> 00:06:26.844
Is that what's best for your individual
business, for your shareholders?

00:06:27.845 --> 00:06:29.138
The third model of A.I.

00:06:29.138 --> 00:06:31.808
consumption is the platform model.

00:06:31.808 --> 00:06:34.268
This is the most comprehensive.

00:06:34.268 --> 00:06:37.814
This is how you become your own
AI firestarter.

00:06:38.439 --> 00:06:42.819
And no, it doesn't mean doing it alone
and reinventing the AI from scratch

00:06:42.819 --> 00:06:47.615
and spending years and millions of dollars
to build your own models.

00:06:48.074 --> 00:06:51.244
With a platform
you have all the elements and ingredients

00:06:51.244 --> 00:06:54.247
in place to build your own AI solutions.

00:06:54.247 --> 00:06:56.124
You have foundation models.

00:06:56.124 --> 00:06:59.127
You have tools to improve
and customize models,

00:06:59.293 --> 00:07:03.548
and you have processes
to build your own tailored AI solutions.

00:07:04.507 --> 00:07:06.801
And importantly, you create

00:07:06.801 --> 00:07:09.804
and accrue value
that is unique to your business.

00:07:10.263 --> 00:07:13.057
Ultimately, I believe that most businesses

00:07:13.057 --> 00:07:15.977
should end up with a mix of all three.

00:07:15.977 --> 00:07:18.980
You'll use third party software
with AI embedded.

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:22.942
Sometimes you'll be totally appropriate
to use someone else's AI,

00:07:23.734 --> 00:07:28.906
but to fully realize the value of AI
and to differentiate yourself from competitors,

00:07:28.906 --> 00:07:33.286
you’ll want a platform approach
to create and own your AI.

00:07:37.665 --> 00:07:39.667
Let me just go a bit deeper

00:07:39.667 --> 00:07:42.795
on AI value creation,
starting with foundation models.

00:07:43.421 --> 00:07:47.091
Foundation models are large scale
deep neural networks trained with

00:07:47.091 --> 00:07:52.805
lots of unlabeled data and subsequently
adapted to many downstream tasks.

00:07:53.181 --> 00:07:57.268
It may be a broad general model,
or it may be a narrower, deeper model,

00:07:57.643 --> 00:08:01.856
but the key is that it is pre-trained
with the expectation

00:08:02.106 --> 00:08:05.860
that you can further enhance it
with your own proprietary data.

00:08:06.194 --> 00:08:08.988
Like when a new employee
joins your business,

00:08:08.988 --> 00:08:13.993
they come in with some general skills
as a foundation and the ability to learn.

00:08:14.619 --> 00:08:17.413
The more they learn about your business,
the more they add

00:08:17.413 --> 00:08:21.209
institutional knowledge and expertise,
the more value they deliver.

00:08:22.001 --> 00:08:25.213
Well, the same is basically true
of our foundation model.

00:08:25.755 --> 00:08:30.009
You use your AI platform to tune it
with your specific business data,

00:08:30.343 --> 00:08:32.803
your proprietary knowledge and expertise,

00:08:32.803 --> 00:08:36.516
and it becomes more expert and
more valuable for your business over time.

00:08:37.475 --> 00:08:40.394
And because you're in
control of the platform and the processes

00:08:40.394 --> 00:08:44.357
and the data, you accrue ever larger
amount of value over time.

00:08:45.316 --> 00:08:48.110
With some of the consumer
AI on the market,

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:52.573
we've already seen some of what happens
when you surrender that control.

00:08:53.074 --> 00:08:55.868
You can get bad data
that leads to bad outcomes.

00:08:55.868 --> 00:08:58.454
You can get hallucinations, basically an

00:08:58.454 --> 00:09:02.333
AI generating very confident
and very incorrect answers.

00:09:02.583 --> 00:09:05.419
You can get into some trouble
for inadvertently

00:09:05.419 --> 00:09:08.422
using someone else's
rights managed content.

00:09:09.131 --> 00:09:11.968
We've even seen proprietary
or sensitive data

00:09:11.968 --> 00:09:15.346
being inadvertently
leaked back into the public spaces.

00:09:15.638 --> 00:09:18.641
That's why
you need to know how your model is built

00:09:18.933 --> 00:09:21.644
and what data was included.

00:09:21.644 --> 00:09:26.315
And it's why tight control of
your sensitive data should be prioritized.

00:09:26.816 --> 00:09:30.236
Strong
AI governance is absolutely critical.

00:09:31.487 --> 00:09:35.032
Yes, now it is the time to jump into AI,

00:09:35.324 --> 00:09:38.619
but please
look before you leap in and ensure

00:09:38.619 --> 00:09:41.956
that you're investing in a smart, safe,
and sustainable approach

00:09:42.248 --> 00:09:45.042
where your business
and your clients and customers

00:09:45.042 --> 00:09:48.045
are the primary beneficiaries.

00:09:51.549 --> 00:09:55.094
There is, I think, a myth about AI right now,

00:09:55.303 --> 00:09:57.888
a basic misunderstanding.

00:09:57.888 --> 00:10:02.101
For the general public generative
AI has seemingly come out of nowhere.

00:10:02.685 --> 00:10:04.353
A lot of people think that there is

00:10:04.353 --> 00:10:07.940
a handful of consumer oriented
AI experiences out there

00:10:08.316 --> 00:10:11.861
and that one model is going to win,
or just a few leaders.

00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:15.740
I don't think that that's
how it's going to play out.

00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:18.743
The future of AI is not about one model,

00:10:18.909 --> 00:10:20.536
it's multi-model.

00:10:20.536 --> 00:10:23.956
Your business will be using multiple
fine tuned models

00:10:23.956 --> 00:10:27.293
to achieve the best results
when applied to specific use cases.

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:30.463
That's why that platform approach
is so important.

00:10:30.713 --> 00:10:35.384
And realistically,
the future of AI is not only proprietary.

00:10:36.135 --> 00:10:39.930
It will also be powered by open science
and open source.

00:10:40.848 --> 00:10:43.559
Proprietary models will play a part.

00:10:43.559 --> 00:10:48.648
But so much of what is going to happen in
the future will not happen behind closed doors.

00:10:49.815 --> 00:10:54.195
It will play out in plain view with full transparency
and accountability

00:10:54.612 --> 00:10:56.781
that open source provides.

00:10:57.365 --> 00:11:01.243
The energy in the open source
community is phenomenal.

00:11:01.577 --> 00:11:06.040
They are distributed projects, university
projects, corporate efforts, all driving

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:09.835
innovation, producing foundation models
that you can tune and deploy

00:11:09.835 --> 00:11:14.131
for your use cases. Hugging Face is 
like GitHub for foundation models.

00:11:14.298 --> 00:11:17.927
And there are over 325,000 open

00:11:17.927 --> 00:11:21.430
source models available
and thousands more being added.

00:11:21.889 --> 00:11:26.310
And this is exactly how it should be
for the good of society in the long term.

00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:30.314
We don't want just one or a few winners,
a few companies

00:11:30.314 --> 00:11:33.693
that can define what AI is and dictate
how it's used.

00:11:34.485 --> 00:11:36.320
But that's not going to happen.

00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:39.407
What we're going to see
is the democratization of AI.

00:11:44.412 --> 00:11:45.162
Okay,

00:11:45.162 --> 00:11:49.750
so I've talked about a lot of different
topics, and I basically told you

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:53.003
that you have a lot of work
to do to be great at AI,

00:11:53.587 --> 00:11:57.967
and maybe that feels overwhelming,
but really that's not my intention.

00:11:58.592 --> 00:12:01.721
My goal is to take down barriers
to participation.

00:12:02.138 --> 00:12:03.556
Not put them up.

00:12:03.556 --> 00:12:06.851
There is a sense of urgency
and fear about waiting

00:12:06.851 --> 00:12:09.854
too long and missing the moment.

00:12:09.854 --> 00:12:10.938
That's okay.

00:12:10.938 --> 00:12:16.026
I assure you that everybody is in the same
situation, feeling the same emotions.

00:12:16.902 --> 00:12:20.322
But I promise that
if instead of rushing into fast

00:12:20.322 --> 00:12:24.577
and easy options to check the box and say,
yes, I put AI in the business,

00:12:25.119 --> 00:12:28.122
if instead you are thoughtful
and deliberate and strategic

00:12:28.456 --> 00:12:32.626
about an AI platform and data management,
and AI governance,

00:12:33.085 --> 00:12:35.838
if you become an AI value creator.

00:12:35.838 --> 00:12:38.924
You're going to be in a position
to succeed over the long term

00:12:39.842 --> 00:12:44.054
and you won't have to start over
every time the wind changes direction.

00:12:44.555 --> 00:12:47.683
You may not have all the products
and processes you need today.

00:12:48.517 --> 00:12:51.520
You may not have all the skills in place.

00:12:51.604 --> 00:12:53.063
That's fine.

00:12:53.063 --> 00:12:55.357
If you're not ready to start alone,

00:12:55.357 --> 00:12:59.278
find a partner that you can trust
and get to work

00:12:59.445 --> 00:13:02.281
so that you can take advantage
of the extraordinary

00:13:02.281 --> 00:13:06.202
opportunities that generative
AI will unlock for your business.

00:13:07.328 --> 00:13:08.496
Personally, I'm

00:13:08.496 --> 00:13:11.499
very excited about this chapter
in technology.

00:13:12.291 --> 00:13:16.545
We, all of us together
are going to use the AI to reshape

00:13:17.046 --> 00:13:20.049
not just our digital world,
but our physical world.

00:13:20.591 --> 00:13:23.844
We are going to use it to help tackle
some of our toughest

00:13:23.844 --> 00:13:27.014
social, medical, environmental problems,
and more.

00:13:27.807 --> 00:13:31.727
We'll do it through science,
but also by empowering businesses

00:13:31.727 --> 00:13:36.190
like yours and mine
to do more, faster and more responsibly.

00:13:36.732 --> 00:13:39.193
Whatever things you do,
you're going to get

00:13:39.193 --> 00:13:42.321
a power full new tool to help
you do them better.

00:13:42.613 --> 00:13:44.740
And its the AI value creators,

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:48.035
that will be
the ones who make the biggest impact.

00:13:48.869 --> 00:13:53.082
It is the value creators who will take
the amazing foundational technology

00:13:53.082 --> 00:13:57.044
that is generative AI and use it to build
entirely new solutions.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:02.800
That's why it is our goal
to make AI accessible to everyone.

00:14:03.467 --> 00:14:04.802
To put it in your hands

00:14:05.803 --> 00:14:06.470
and I can't

00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:09.473
wait to see what you will do with it.

00:14:09.473 --> 00:14:12.810
Thank you
for watching this episode of AI Academy.

00:14:13.519 --> 00:14:17.857
I hope you will join us again as our IBM
experts take you on deeper dives

00:14:18.107 --> 00:14:21.610
into everything that a business leader
needs to know about AI.

